# Build-time configuration for the BA bot widget.
#
# Both values are NEXT_PUBLIC_*, which means Next inlines them into the client
# bundle and ships them to every visitor. They are public by construction, so
# they are committed here rather than held as CI secrets — that keeps the
# Cloudflare Pages build working with no extra configuration.
#
# The real secrets (LLM_API_KEY, TURNSTILE_SECRET, IP_HASH_SALT, RESEND_API_KEY)
# live only in the Worker, pushed from 1Password by
# apps/ba-bot-api/scripts/sync-secrets.sh. None of them belong in this file.

# Worker origin. A custom domain (api.unodigit.com.au) needs the zone hosted on
# Cloudflare; DNS is currently at OnlyDomains, so this stays on workers.dev.
# EMPTY ON PURPOSE — it means same-origin, and the widget reads it that way.
# public/_worker.js proxies /api/* from www.unodigit.com.au to the bot Worker at
# the edge, so the browser never issues a cross-origin request and the Worker's
# hostname never reaches the client bundle. Setting an absolute origin here
# would undo the proxy and put it back.
NEXT_PUBLIC_BA_BOT_URL=

# Turnstile *site* key (the public half). The secret half is a Worker secret.
NEXT_PUBLIC_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=0x4AAAAAAET8RNKDwLGdBrG-
